  "request": {
    "input": "search_document: I understand your frustration, but I cannot grant an exception to the policy regarding misuse claims based on the provided handbook excerpts.\n\nAccording to the **Damaged Items** section, if damage is caused by improper use, the claim will be denied [damaged_items.4]. The handbook states that Northwind Outdoor reserves the right to inspect the item upon return, and if the inspection reveals signs of misuse or neglect, the claim is denied, and the customer is responsible for return shipping costs [damaged_items.4].\n\nAdditionally, the handbook specifies that to initiate a valid damage claim, you must report visible damage within **48 hours** of delivery and provide at least 3 high-resolution photos showing the defect, the overall item, and the packaging [damaged_items.1]. It explicitly states that failure to provide this visual evidence within the 48-hour window results in an automatic denial because the company cannot verify the condition of the item after it has been used or stored [damaged_items.1].\n\nSince you mentioned the tent was \"set up once\" before the damage was discovered, this likely falls under the \"used or stored\" condition that prevents verification of the original state, leading to the classification of misuse or denial due to lack of timely evidence [damaged_items.1]. The handbook does not provide a mechanism for overriding these specific denial criteria for first-time buyers or for accepting returns classified as misuse.\n\nAs the handbook excerpts do not cover a process for appealing a \"misuse\" denial or granting exceptions to the 48-hour reporting/verification rule, I must offer to escalate this ticket to a human agent who may have access to further review options or senior support teams mentioned for manual reviews [damaged_items.2].\n\nWould you like me to escalate this ticket to a human agent?",
    "model": "nomic-embed-text",
